WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
AI can write a business plan. It can

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.360
even these days design a logo. And I

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:07.560
know that there are tools out there that

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.200
also can build a website. But can I

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.160
actually build something that people

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.720
want? Well, today we're going to find

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:15.440
out. I thought it would be fun to give

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:17.120
complete control over to AI for building

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.720
and coming up with my next business. And

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.560
whatever happens, I'm going to follow

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.520
its advice. Now, to make this fair, I

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:25.960
came up with a few simple rules. One, AI

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.120
picks a business. Two, AI chooses the

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.800
target audience. Three, AI decides the

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:33.400
branding. Four, AI builds the market

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.360
strategy. And five, AI writes the launch

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.360
plan. If I ever hit a point where I need

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.600
to make a decision, I head over to AI to

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.920
help make that decision for me. And then

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.280
I execute. And just as a little

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.520
disclaimer, the only thing I'm going to

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.760
ignore is if AI suggests anything

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.800
illegal, unethical, or financially

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.200
irresponsible. Otherwise, I am trusting

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.920
the robot. For me, success is not about

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.560
making a million dollars. I am a

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.960
stay-at-home mom, and I really just want

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.000
to be bringing in a little bit of extra

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.480
cash for my family. So, if AI can build

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:03.240
me something that is a true source of

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.000
income for me, that generates even just

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.520
a few dollars a month, then I think it

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.080
is worth it. So, first things first,

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:10.600
we're going to just go ahead, head over

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.600
to ChatGPT, and ask it what business we

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.840
should build. So, ChatGPT has given me a

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:16.920
few fun examples. AI marketing studio

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:18.960
for small brands, build the business

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.220
toolkit for moms, done with you AI

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.200
business coaching, build an SEO content

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:24.720
[clears throat] business, creator

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.160
business academy, AI prompt library

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.560
subscription.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.680
I'm not too sure about that. Business in

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.000
a box kit. So, those were a few

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.680
different it gave me. Some maybe better

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.080
than others. So, I'm actually going to

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.080
go with this first idea here because I

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.280
felt like that is the most aligned with

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:43.320
myself, my passions, and what I have

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.000
experience doing. But before I spend

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.040
weeks building out this business, I

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.880
wanted to know something that AI didn't

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.880
necessarily have an answer for. The

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:52.640
question is, does anyone actually even

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:55.040
want this? Well, that's where a really

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.400
cool tool called Semrush comes in. This

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.560
portion of the video is sponsored by

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.680
Semrush. And honestly, it fits perfectly

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.520
into this experiment because while I do

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:05.200
think that AI is great at generating

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.560
ideas, it's a lot tougher for AI to

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:10.080
validate those ideas. And I think that

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.000
this tool is much more useful and

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.520
helpful in determining whether an idea

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.200
is actually going to be worthwhile. I

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.440
think that one of the biggest mistakes

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:20.400
people make when starting a new business

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.000
through using AI, they get the idea from

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.920
AI. And because of that, they just

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.760
assume that it's automatically a really

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.760
good business opportunity. But the truth

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:30.240
is that idea needs demand. It needs

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.760
customers, you know, people to actually

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.840
buy your products. And it needs a

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:35.200
realistic path to getting discovered. So

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.320
that is actually where I am using

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:38.920
Semrush. Instead of relying on AI's

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:41.120
confidence, I wanted to see what the

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:42.720
actual search data had to say. I started

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.240
by checking whether people were actually

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:45.840
searching for this topic. How many

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.880
searches does it get every single month?

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.800
Is interest growing, staying flat, or

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:51.560
declining? Then I looked at keyword

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:54.160
difficulty. And by the way, if you don't

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.400
know what keywords to search on Semrush,

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.320
you can always ask ChatGPT.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.280
So the first keyword I chose to search

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.720
was AI marketing services because this

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.160
falls within the niche that I was

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:05.920
thinking about. But when I look at the

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.200
keyword difficulty, it is 64%, which

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.440
actually tells me that I would need to

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.560
have 210 referring domains and optimize

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.560
content to compete on this keyword. So

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:17.000
that's not super great. Another keyword

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:18.640
that ChatGPT recommended was fractional

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.720
marketing manager. So I searched that

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:22.720
one next. Now it says that the keyword

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.519
difficulty is actually quite easy, that

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.280
it's very likely I would get ranked for

00:03:24.519 --> 00:03:28.200
this keyword. Realistically, this is

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.160
going to tell me if a brand new website

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.920
is going to actually be able to compete

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:34.000
with a more established website or

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.080
domain. Or would I be going up against

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:38.600
companies that have been dominating the

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.640
space for years? From there, I explored

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:42.680
related keywords, questions people are

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:44.120
asking, and adjacent topics that I

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.959
hadn't even considered yet. This

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.400
actually gave me a much clearer picture

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:49.640
of what my customers actually care

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.519
about, not just what AI thought they

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:53.520
might care about. Finally, I analyzed

00:03:51.519 --> 00:03:55.120
the competitors already dominating the

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.760
space. What pages bring them the most

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:58.480
traffic? Where are the gaps and what are

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.360
the best opportunities for a business in

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:02.720
this space? That alone made me rethink

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.160
part of AI's original recommendation.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.160
But what I thought was especially

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.320
interesting was how this fit into where

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.360
search is actually going. For years,

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:12.560
marketers and even consumers have relied

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:14.600
heavily on Google. Today, more people

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:17.079
are turning to AI tools like Perplexity

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:18.880
or even ChatGPT or Claude to compare

00:04:17.079 --> 00:04:20.799
products, compare brands, and get

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.640
recommendations. Search behavior is

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:23.960
actually really changing. And that means

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:26.080
marketers have to think differently,

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:28.880
too. And that's why Semrush recently

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.600
introduced its MCP integration with

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.800
Perplexity. This way, instead of

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:34.440
switching back and forth between

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.560
different tools, I can access Semrush's

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:38.440
search intelligence directly within

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:40.640
Perplexity. This is especially helpful

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:43.120
when I am brainstorming, researching,

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:45.200
and asking AI all sorts of questions.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.040
This means that AI is not just

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.840
generating ideas based on what sounds

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.000
good, it's generating ideas based on

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:53.320
real search intelligence, as well as

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.080
competitive research and keyword data.

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.840
For an experiment like this, where AI is

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.720
making every important business

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:00.919
decision, that's actually incredibly

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.919
valuable and extremely time-saving. It

00:05:00.919 --> 00:05:04.919
turns AI into a much smarter

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:07.080
collaborator because the recommendations

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:09.000
are grounded in actual market data

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.320
instead of pure speculation. So, if

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.040
you're curious about starting a new

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.640
business and you want to make sure that

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.560
it's actually going to be successful,

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.360
you need a little help with your

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:18.280
keywords and more, and you're curious

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:20.880
how your business would show up in both

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:21.960
organic search and AI hard search, or

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.120
you just want to make better marketing

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:26.280
decisions backed up by real data,

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.440
definitely check out Semrush One, linked

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.080
down in the description [music] box.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.160
Now, let's see if AI actually chose a

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.880
business worth building. At this point,

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.560
there is really no turning back. The

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.640
idea had passed what I considered the

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.680
first major test. There was actual

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:41.360
search demand and the competition looked

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:44.080
pretty manageable. So, now I wasn't just

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.120
building a business that sounded good in

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:48.000
an AI chat window. Now came the part I

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:49.880
was honestly the most curious about.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.600
Could AI build something that felt like

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:53.520
a legitimate business? So from here

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:55.600
forward, every major decision was going

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:57.240
to be done by AI. The name, the

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.280
branding, the website, the messaging,

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:02.120
and even how we plan to acquire

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:04.000
customers. My role was not to outsmart

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:06.240
it or even improve the ideas, it was

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:07.920
really to execute. So the first

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:09.600
challenge was coming up with the name. I

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.240
quickly realized this was harder than

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:13.280
expected. A business name isn't

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:15.320
something that just sounds cool. It has

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:17.800
to be memorable, easy to spell,

00:06:15.320 --> 00:06:19.360
available as a domain, and ideally tell

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.560
people something about what the business

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:23.880
actually does. So of course I asked AI

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:25.960
to generate me a list of ideas. Some of

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.400
the suggestions were surprisingly good.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:29.720
Others were exactly what you would

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:31.640
expect AI to sound like, you know,

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:33.640
generic buzzwords mashed together. I

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:35.440
found myself laughing at a few of them,

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:37.160
but eventually one name kept standing

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:38.760
out. It wasn't flashy, but it felt

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:39.880
believable. More importantly, it felt

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:42.120
like a company that could actually

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:43.560
exist. Instead of just choosing a name

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:45.480
and going with it, I actually pushed a

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:47.040
little bit further and asked AI why it

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:48.840
chose that name. What emotions was it

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.800
trying to evoke? What type of customer

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:53.040
is it speaking to? And those follow-up

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:54.600
questions I think actually helped create

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:56.440
a better answer than the original

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:57.960
prompt. With a name selected, it was

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.600
time to build an identity around it.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:01.040
This is where AI really started to

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.600
surprise me. Within minutes it

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:05.080
recommended brand voice, assets, colors,

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.840
imagery, and even the overall

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:08.960
personality. But instead of simply

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:10.440
asking AI to design a logo, I wanted to

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.400
understand the reasoning behind each

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:14.560
recommendation. Why should the brand

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:16.880
feel more modern versus playful? Why

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:19.400
choose blue over green or yellow over

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.720
orange? Why it position the company as

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:23.800
approachable rather than premium? Those

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:25.160
explanations really helped transform

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:27.160
what could have been random design

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:29.320
suggestions into something that actually

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:31.280
resembled a professional creative brief.

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:33.080
The more I interacted with AI, the more

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:35.160
I realized the quality of the outputs

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.880
depend entirely on the quality of my

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:38.800
question. When I gave it vague prompts,

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:40.760
it gave me generic answers. But when I

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.600
asked it to justify its decisions and

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:44.280
think like an experimental brand

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.040
strategist, the responses became

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.360
dramatically more useful. With the

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.960
branding complete, it was time to build

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:51.680
something that people could actually

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:53.400
visit, aka my website. So, I asked AI to

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.960
create the structure for the homepage

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:57.000
including the headline, value

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:58.720
proposition, calls to action, frequently

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.440
asked questions, and anything else that

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.640
it felt should be included. This was

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.720
probably the point where I actually was

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:05.680
the most impressed. At this point, AI

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.960
wasn't just writing a wall of text, it

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:08.640
was actually thinking through the

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:10.320
customer journey. It explained what

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:12.240
information should appear first, what

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:14.120
objectives visitors might have, and how

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.720
to guide somebody from curiosity to

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:17.400
actually taking action. That doesn't

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:19.160
mean it was perfect. In fact, one thing

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:21.280
that AI recommended was including

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.640
customer testimonials, but of course, as

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:24.280
a brand new business, I don't actually

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:26.000
have those yet. This is a good reminder

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.640
that AI can optimize and create

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:29.560
something convincing rather than what's

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.520
actually true. And this has become one

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:33.159
of my biggest lessons with using AI.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:35.360
It's not something that you rely on

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:37.440
100%, but it's definitely a great tool

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.280
to collaborate with. So, now that our

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:41.200
business exists, we have a much bigger

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:43.120
problem. How do we actually convince

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.920
people to buy it and find it in the

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:46.880
first place? I think this is where a lot

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.680
of online businesses fail. Building and

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.320
creating something can be really fun and

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:52.080
exciting, but getting people to actually

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:53.760
discover your product, especially if

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:55.520
it's a really awesome and exciting

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:57.400
product that you put a lot of time and

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:59.360
energy into, that's actually the hardest

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:00.480
part. So, once again, I turned to AI and

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:02.839
asked it how it would launch this

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.360
company if it was starting from zero. It

00:09:02.839 --> 00:09:06.320
came up with a surprisingly

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:08.560
comprehensive plan that include things

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:10.640
from SEO, content marketing, social

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:12.600
media, email marketing, partnerships,

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:14.360
and several other growth channels that I

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:16.080
thought were really interesting. Others

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:18.200
may have been a little too optimistic,

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:19.800
but again, we're using AI as a thought

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.520
partner here. Instead of accepting

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.600
everything at face value, I started

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:25.280
challenging its assumptions. Why this

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:27.320
platform instead of another? Why this

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:29.040
audience? Why would somebody buy from us

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:31.040
versus a competitor? I feel that these

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:32.720
conversations produced far more

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.880
thoughtful conversations and helped me

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:38.400
come to stronger conclusions. And again,

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.336
it reinforced this piece that AI doesn't

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:41.920
replace critical thinking. It actually

00:09:40.336 --> 00:09:44.040
[clears throat] rewards it. Going into

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:45.840
this experiment, I assumed AI would save

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.560
me a lot of time by creating content

